per day |\n| 6 | ×0.95 | ×0.845 | Under-orders both items; likely the worst |\n\n- **Plan 0** orders every 2 days, roughly at the average forecast. It saves the 39 fee on about 12 days but carries an extra night of stock. That stock costs about 50 per pair of days against 39 saved, so it nets out close to plan 2.\n- **Plan 3** orders a flat 22 / 55 every day. That is too much item 1 early, when demand is in the 40s, and too little late, around the 102 spike on day 19. It probably lands in the middle.\n- **Plan 5** orders every 3 days, so it pays more for storage. The batches arriving on days 20 and 26 are 259 and 251 units, which exceed the 224 capacity, and the excess is lost. It is probably near the bottom.\n\nMy expected top four are 7, 4 and 2, with the fourth place a close call among 0, 1 and 3."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5058, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5058}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:00:36.203Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWB88hfvnYgN7APfexRL"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JtCYP3ybogXu2R8XqcsUn6", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWB88v4cWHCnxQK2JCzt", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JtCYP3ybogXu2R8XqcsUn6", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [